{
  "info": {
    "name": "Thriftpedia - Order & Single-Stock",
    "description": "Order module requests. Run against a LOCAL server/DB only: the run leaves productId SOLD (completed order).\nBefore running set buyerAToken, buyerBToken, adminToken, productId and productId2 (two AVAILABLE products).\nRun top to bottom: later requests use orderId/orderId2/orderNumber saved by earlier ones.\nStatus flow: PENDING -> PROCESSING|CANCELLED; PROCESSING -> SHIPPED|CANCELLED; SHIPPED -> COMPLETED. COMPLETED and CANCELLED are terminal.\nThe runner is sequential, so it does not prove concurrency; use scripts/concurrent-purchase.js (10 parallel checkouts) for that.\nPATCH /api/orders/:orderId is a deprecated alias of PATCH /api/orders/:orderId/status.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health Check",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "POST /api/orders",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create order (buyer A) - 201",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"orderId\", d._id); pm.collectionVariables.set(\"orderNumber\", d.orderNumber); }",
                  "pm.test(\"Order is PENDING\", () => pm.expect(d.status).to.eql(\"PENDING\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"orderNumber is TP-XXXX\", () => pm.expect(d.orderNumber).to.match(/^TP-\\d{4,}$/));",
                  "pm.test(\"total equals product snapshot price\", () => pm.expect(d.total).to.eql(d.productSnapshot.price));",
                  "pm.test(\"buyerSnapshot is stored\", () => pm.expect(d.buyerSnapshot).to.have.keys(\"name\", \"email\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"history starts with PENDING\", () => pm.expect(d.statusHistory.map((h) => h.status)).to.eql([\"PENDING\"]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{buyerAToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
